WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:04.240
The second official trailer for "Venom:&nbsp;
Let There Be Carnage" has finally landed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:07.040
and we've been treated to a&nbsp;
heaping serving of new content.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.640
There are also a few hidden easter eggs that&nbsp;
are fun to dissect, so let's take a look at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:14.480
the small details you may have missed in the&nbsp;
second "Venom: Let There Be Carnage" trailer.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.240
During the trailer, Eddie Brock sits&nbsp;
down at his desk and looks at a Daily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.560
Bugle article on his computer, where Cletus&nbsp;
Kasady is making headlines for his crimes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:26.320
While he looks over the report, some drawings&nbsp;
are scattered in front of him on his desk.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.640
Written inside the trunk of&nbsp;
a large tree are the words

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.120
"to thee the strife was&nbsp;
given between the suffering."

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.520
Poets and literary enthusiasts will recognize this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:36.160
as a part of a stanza in&nbsp;
Lord Byron's "Prometheus".

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:40.640
"Prometheus" is about the Greek Titan of the same&nbsp;
name. Known as the God of Fire and a trickster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:44.880
he often helped humanity by stealing fire and&nbsp;
giving it to humans. A traitor to the gods,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:48.640
and a friend of humans, Prometheus&nbsp;
was punished by Zeus for his "crimes."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:52.720
The poem primarily focuses on what happens&nbsp;
when one resists tyranny and how powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:56.640
that is. It'll be quite interesting to see&nbsp;
how this quote directly connects to Cletus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.440
as well as why it's something that&nbsp;
Eddie appears to be analyzing.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:03.440
The new trailer also references The Daily&nbsp;
Bugle, Marvel's most famous in-universe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:07.200
newspaper. Since Peter Parker and Eddie Brock&nbsp;
both worked for the company in the comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.240
it isn't surprising that the sequel&nbsp;
calls back to the publication.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:13.520
Detective Mulligan is reading a copy of&nbsp;
the paper in the first trailer, and the new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:17.920
footage shows Eddie working on his exclusive&nbsp;
interview with Cletus Kassady for the Bugle.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:25.920
"When I get outta here, and I&nbsp;
will, it's gonna be carnage."

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:29.440
The layout of the paper's next edition is&nbsp;
shown on Eddie's laptop, using the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:33.120
logo design as the Sam Raimi "Spider-Man"&nbsp;
trilogy. But the paper's masthead also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:38.000
reads "West Coast Edition," so clearly the New&nbsp;
York-based outlet has expanded across the U.S.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:41.200
This honors Eddie's comics backstory&nbsp;
while also keeping him away from New&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:44.240
York so that Sony doesn't have to&nbsp;
explain where Spider-Man is yet.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:48.960
Aside from all the Symbiote shenanigans, the&nbsp;
trailer also gives fans a better look at Naomie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:53.360
Harris as Shriek, locked up in the Ravencroft&nbsp;
Institute for the Criminally Insane before Woody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:57.520
Harrelson's Carnage breaks her out. Harris briefly&nbsp;
appeared in the first trailer for the sequel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:00.880
which showed Shriek's glowing eye as&nbsp;
she's curled up in her Ravencroft cell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:05.120
but this new footage gives us a better look at&nbsp;
her ear-piercing powers. The villain unleashes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:09.280
a devastating scream in a car, smashing&nbsp;
the windshield. This is probably after her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:13.200
escape from the institute since she's still&nbsp;
dressed in the same white detention outfit.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.800
Shriek is a mutant in the comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:17.920
but it's not clear if this version of the&nbsp;
character will have the Mutant Gene/X-Gene&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:22.960
in the "Venom" sequel because Marvel Studios&nbsp;
now holds the rights to mutants and the X-Men.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:27.280
Shriek's eye is also glowing bright blue as she's&nbsp;
screaming in the new trailer, which could actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:32.080
be a nod to another surprising ability she has.&nbsp;
Not only can she unleash a sonic scream, she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:36.480
can draw out someone's inner darkness using her&nbsp;
"Dark Empathy" which causes her victims to commit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:40.800
unspeakable acts. Since she'll be partnering up&nbsp;
with Woody Harrelson's Carnage, it wouldn't be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:45.280
surprising if she helps turn San Francisco&nbsp;
upside down using her manipulative skills.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:48.400
In several trailer scenes, Eddie Brock&nbsp;
is seen wearing a tee-shirt underneath&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:52.240
his jacket that reads "Mumford Phys. Ed.&nbsp;
Dept." Fans of "Beverly Hills Cop" should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:56.160
recognize this shirt immediately, as Eddie&nbsp;
Murphy wears a similar shirt in the R-rated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:00.240
'80s film. Murphy's character Axel Foley is an&nbsp;
alumnus of the real-life Detroit high school,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.800
and he wears a white and grey&nbsp;
version of the shirt in the film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:06.960
In fact, "Beverly Hills Cop" producer Jerry&nbsp;
Bruckheimer graduated from the school as well.

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:10.880
The directors of "Beverly Hills Cop 4"&nbsp;
revealed in 2017 that they would love&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:15.120
to have either Hardy or Channing Tatum as the&nbsp;
sequel's main antagonist. Is this Hardy's way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:19.600
of telling us he's been cast or is interested&nbsp;
in the film? Probably not, but here's hoping.

